WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.025 --> 00:00:15.507
stared at the hot sauce overflowing the pot.

2
00:00:15.527 --> 00:00:18.209
"Why is the hot sauce growing?"

3
00:00:18.469 --> 00:00:19.010
he cried.

4
00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:21.832
Waldo was fumbling with his glasses.

5
00:00:24.654 --> 00:00:27.677
He jumped back as some hot sauce oozed onto his shoe.

6
00:00:27.697 --> 00:00:30.339
"I—I don't know!"

7
00:00:30.719 --> 00:00:31.520
the wizard said.

8
00:00:31.956 --> 00:00:35.079
He put his glasses on and picked up the jar of enhancer.

9
00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:38.943
He peered at the label and then slapped himself on the forehead.

10
00:00:38.963 --> 00:00:41.185
"This isn't enhancer!

11
00:00:41.205 --> 00:00:43.267
It's expander."

12
00:00:43.287 --> 00:00:45.950
"What does expander do?"

13
00:00:46.270 --> 00:00:46.991
Ben asked.

14
00:00:47.011 --> 00:00:48.993
"What do you think it does?"

15
00:00:49.394 --> 00:00:50.134
Waldo said.

16
00:00:50.154 --> 00:00:53.678
"It expands things—it makes them bigger!"

17
00:00:53.698 --> 00:01:02.004
"Ugh." Ben watched helplessly as the sauce flowed across the floor toward a cabinet.

18
00:01:02.024 --> 00:01:06.388
"What are we going to do?"

19
00:01:07.289 --> 00:01:08.189
Waldo sighed.

20
00:01:08.209 --> 00:01:12.693
"It'll stop in a few minutes—when the pot is empty."

21
00:01:13.354 --> 00:01:14.234
Waldo was right.

22
00:01:14.675 --> 00:01:16.636
Soon the sauce stopped expanding.

23
00:01:19.379 --> 00:01:20.680
Ben grabbed some rags.

24
00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:25.224
"We'd better clean up this mess."

25
00:01:27.392 --> 00:01:34.854
Waldo found a mop, and ten minutes later the floor was clean.

26
00:01:38.075 --> 00:01:42.256
Waldo ladled out some hot sauce from the pot and poured it into a small bottle.

27
00:01:45.937 --> 00:01:46.958
He handed it to Ben.

28
00:01:48.098 --> 00:01:51.459
"Put this in your food tomorrow in Cooking class," the wizard said.

29
00:01:51.479 --> 00:01:55.420
"By the time the bell rings, you'll be out of the cooking competition.

30
00:01:56.308 --> 00:01:58.550
Now we have just one more thing to do."

31
00:01:58.570 --> 00:02:00.351
"We're not done?"

32
00:02:00.811 --> 00:02:01.512
Ben asked.

33
00:02:01.532 --> 00:02:04.093
"Nope," Waldo said.

34
00:02:04.113 --> 00:02:06.955
"You need a backup plan, just in case Mr.

35
00:02:07.035 --> 00:02:08.396
Icky likes spicy food."

36
00:02:10.457 --> 00:02:12.899
He pulled his large spell book out of his backpack.

37
00:02:12.919 --> 00:02:17.102
"What kind of spell are you looking for?"

38
00:02:17.522 --> 00:02:18.263
Ben asked.

39
00:02:20.124 --> 00:02:23.406
"How about a spell that makes your food explode?"

40
00:02:23.426 --> 00:02:27.005
"That won't work," Ben said.

41
00:02:27.025 --> 00:02:29.226
"Everyone loves exploding food."

42
00:02:29.246 --> 00:02:32.128
"People don't," Waldo said.

43
00:02:32.148 --> 00:02:36.892
"Mayor Hubbletree was furious when those pizzas exploded, remember?"

44
00:02:38.413 --> 00:02:39.153
Ben shrugged.

45
00:02:39.754 --> 00:02:40.334
"But Mr.

46
00:02:40.454 --> 00:02:41.715
Icky won't mind that.

47
00:02:42.476 --> 00:02:47.899
I need something that will convince him I'm not good enough to be on Kids' Kitchen Showdown."

48
00:02:47.919 --> 00:02:52.323
"Right." Waldo flipped through more pages.

49
00:02:52.343 --> 00:02:54.044
"Here's a good one.

50
00:02:55.668 --> 00:02:58.931
With this spell, any food you touch will disappear."

51
00:02:58.951 --> 00:03:01.453
"That's no good," Ben said.

52
00:03:01.473 --> 00:03:03.695
"I need to cook bad food.

53
00:03:03.795 --> 00:03:04.716
Not no food."

54
00:03:04.736 --> 00:03:09.159
"Hmm." Waldo examined another page in his book.

55
00:03:09.179 --> 00:03:13.943
"What if everything you cooked smelled like rotting garbage?"

56
00:03:13.963 --> 00:03:16.926
"What would be so bad about that?"

57
00:03:17.246 --> 00:03:17.967
Ben asked.

58
00:03:17.987 --> 00:03:20.909
"I guess nothing," Waldo said.

59
00:03:21.390 --> 00:03:23.972
He turned another page and bent down over his book.

60
00:03:24.532 --> 00:03:26.153
"Oh, this would be perfect.

61
00:03:26.793 --> 00:03:28.113
Rotting fish!"

62
00:03:28.133 --> 00:03:31.274
"Eww," Ben said.

63
00:03:31.294 --> 00:03:33.595
"That's disgusting."

64
00:03:33.615 --> 00:03:36.676
"It sure is," Waldo agreed.

65
00:03:36.696 --> 00:03:40.717
"Everyone hates the smell of rotting fish—even monsters."

66
00:03:41.597 --> 00:03:42.317
Ben nodded.

67
00:03:42.337 --> 00:03:43.317
"Let's do it."

68
00:03:45.558 --> 00:03:49.239
Waldo studied the spell for a moment, quietly murmuring the words.

69
00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:51.680
Finally he stood up.

70
00:03:52.780 --> 00:03:55.002
He pulled out his wand and pointed it at Ben.

71
00:03:55.802 --> 00:04:00.025
As Waldo muttered the magical words, green light flashed from his wand.

72
00:04:02.147 --> 00:04:04.588
Ben felt a strange, tingling sensation.

73
00:04:04.608 --> 00:04:08.471
"Did it work?"

74
00:04:08.491 --> 00:04:11.093
"Probably," Waldo said.

75
00:04:11.113 --> 00:04:14.835
"But we won't know until you cook some—" Waldo sniffed.

76
00:04:16.617 --> 00:04:18.358
"Ugh! What's that smell?"

77
00:04:18.998 --> 00:04:19.759
Ben sniffed.

78
00:04:22.688 --> 00:04:23.488
"I think it's me."

79
00:04:24.889 --> 00:04:25.850
He smelled his arm.

80
00:04:25.870 --> 00:04:28.651
"Oh no!

81
00:04:29.151 --> 00:04:29.952
It is me!

82
00:04:30.432 --> 00:04:31.833
I smell like rotting fish!

83
00:04:32.673 --> 00:04:37.075
You messed up the spell—you made me smell like rotting fish!"

84
00:04:38.116 --> 00:04:40.757
"Oops." Waldo looked in his spell book.

85
00:04:40.777 --> 00:04:42.798
"I wonder what I did wrong."

86
00:04:43.738 --> 00:04:44.959
Just then Mr.

87
00:04:45.019 --> 00:04:46.320
Freaky made an announcement.

88
00:04:47.224 --> 00:04:50.026
"Mr. Bog is going to lock the doors in ten minutes.

89
00:04:50.547 --> 00:04:53.129
All students must leave the building at once."

90
00:04:54.630 --> 00:04:55.450
Ben sighed.

91
00:04:55.490 --> 00:04:58.032
"We have to go home, Waldo."

92
00:05:01.194 --> 00:05:05.698
As Ben floated into the corridor, a few monsters immediately cleared out of his way.

93
00:05:05.718 --> 00:05:09.140
"Yuck!" a mummy said.

94
00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:11.182
A ghoul covered her nose.

95
00:05:11.202 --> 00:05:13.744
"What smells so bad?"

96
00:05:15.100 --> 00:05:17.241
A fish monster didn't mind the smell though.

97
00:05:17.261 --> 00:05:20.662
"Mmm! It smells like my cousin's house!"

98
00:05:21.602 --> 00:05:24.203
Ben was glad that Winnie wasn't anywhere in sight.

99
00:05:25.663 --> 00:05:28.224
But as he hurried toward an exit, he spotted her.

100
00:05:29.984 --> 00:05:32.665
She must have stayed after school for broom-flying practice.

101
00:05:41.627 --> 00:05:43.948
"Ben!" Winnie ran to catch up to him.

102
00:05:44.352 --> 00:05:46.453
When she reached him, she covered her nose.

103
00:05:46.473 --> 00:05:49.815
"What's that horrible smell?"

104
00:05:49.835 --> 00:05:52.957
"It's me," Ben blurted out.

105
00:05:52.977 --> 00:05:56.999
"Waldo was trying to cast a spell, but he didn't do it right."

106
00:05:57.019 --> 00:05:59.040
"What kind of spell?"

107
00:06:00.401 --> 00:06:05.724
Ben watched the expression on Winnie's face change as he explained about the hot sauce and the rotten

108
00:06:05.804 --> 00:06:06.444
fish spell.

109
00:06:08.185 --> 00:06:10.346
Right away he knew she didn't approve.

110
00:06:10.366 --> 00:06:12.908
"I can't believe you'd do that, Ben!

111
00:06:13.548 --> 00:06:16.609
Do you know how many kids would love to be on that show?

112
00:06:17.809 --> 00:06:19.530
Monsters are jealous of you.

113
00:06:19.990 --> 00:06:22.591
And here you are, trying to sabotage yourself.

114
00:06:24.451 --> 00:06:25.451
You should be ashamed!"

115
00:06:26.712 --> 00:06:29.252
Ben sighed, staring down at the ground.

116
00:06:29.272 --> 00:06:35.114
"Mr. Icky picked you for a reason," Winnie went on.

117
00:06:35.134 --> 00:06:37.375
"You have to compete.

118
00:06:38.075 --> 00:06:39.075
It's the right thing to do."

119
00:06:40.035 --> 00:06:40.756
Ben sighed.

120
00:06:43.448 --> 00:06:44.370
"You're right, Winnie.

121
00:06:44.991 --> 00:06:45.832
I'll do the show."

122
00:06:47.134 --> 00:06:48.036
Winnie smiled.

123
00:06:48.056 --> 00:06:50.680
"Good!" Ben sniffed.

124
00:06:50.700 --> 00:06:55.408
"But right now I need to get home and take a shower!"
